## Verification

Confirm the cluster is actually healthy before treating this deployment as
complete -- generating the scripts is not the same as having a working
cluster:

- `erlite cluster status` should show all {{len .Config.Nodes}} nodes active
  and healthy.
- Each node's `https://<node>:{{.Config.APIPort}}/v1/ready` should return
  HTTP 200 with `"status":"ready"`. A 503 means that node's workers or
  catalog view aren't ready yet -- wait and retry rather than assuming
  something is broken.
- Losing more than {{.Config.ReplicationFactor}} minus {{.Quorum}} node(s) is
  expected to reject consistent writes outright, not silently degrade them --
  that is correct behavior, not a bug, if you're testing failure handling.
{{range .Verification}}
