## Upgrade procedure

Erlite performs a release-compatibility preflight on every `join` -- an
incompatible node is rejected before it can affect cluster membership. To
roll out an upgrade:

1. Upgrade one node at a time, starting with a follower, never the current
   leader.
2. After each node restarts, confirm it rejoins and `erlite cluster status`
   shows it healthy before moving to the next node.
3. Upgrade the current leader last; it will fail over naturally, or you can
   transfer leadership away from it first if you want to control the timing.
